        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "The centres of the six faces of a cube of side \\(a\\) are joined to form a regular octahedron. The ratio of the surface area of this octahedron to its volume is",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The octahedron has eight equilateral triangular faces, each of side \\(a/\\\\sqrt2\\). Hence \\(S=8\\\\cdot\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt3}{4}\\\\cdot\\\\frac{a^2}{2}=\\\\sqrt3a^2\\). It consists of two square pyramids with common base area \\(a^2/2\\) and height \\(a/2\\), so \\(V=a^3/6\\). Therefore \\(\\\\frac{S}{V}=\\\\frac{6\\\\sqrt3}{a}\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
